    "Carpinteria compresses the whole coastal-appliance problem into a few walkable blocks. The town's grid runs right down to the sand, so there's no 'inland side' to hide on — from the Linden Avenue cottages to Sandyland Cove and the Padaro Lane stretch, everything mechanical lives in salt-bearing air.",
    "What that does, concretely: condenser coils corrode and load up until refrigerators run near-constantly. Door gaskets stiffen and split years early, feeding humid air into freezer compartments that then frost over. Outdoor grill igniters — a beach-house staple — corrode into that familiar endless clicking. Garage appliances fare worst of all, because coastal garages breathe with the weather. None of this is exotic to us; it's the same physics we service in coastal LA, concentrated into one very pleasant town.",
    "The practical answer isn't buying 'marine grade' everything — it's maintenance timing. Coils cleaned on a 4–6 month cycle, gaskets checked annually, grills serviced before the season instead of during it. On every Carpinteria call we look at the coastal wear items while we're there, because the second failure is usually already visible during the first."
